---
/* -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Visitation, phone & staying in contact.

   Phone and visiting policy comes up on 23 of 571 Buena Vista calls (4.0%
   declarative) — modest volume, but it is a decision-blocking question for both
   the patient and the family, which is why it earns a page rather than a line.

   FACTS AND THEIR SOURCE — all from admissions on recorded calls:
     "you get access to your phone or electronics from 4PM to 9PM once you're
      on residential"
     "You also get your cell phone every night from 4PM to 9PM"
     "There is visitation, which is on Wednesday, Saturday, and Sunday."
     Sponsors can come into the facility and do step work.
     Phone access is tied to residential, not detox.

   ⚠ THE HOURS ARE NOT SETTLED. One agent quotes 4:30-8:30pm rather than 4-9pm,
   and the wiki says 4-10pm. The page therefore says "roughly 4-9pm", pairs
   every specific with "confirm on the call", and the hero carries an explicit
   note that arrangements get adjusted. Do not harden these into exact times
   without checking with the programme — and if you do confirm them, update
   here and tell admissions so the phone script matches.

   Visiting days (Wed/Sat/Sun) are stated with more confidence because they were
   given plainly and unambiguously.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import TopBar from '../../components/TopBar.astro';
import Nav from '../../components/Nav.astro';

import ContactHero from '../../components/contact/ContactHero.astro';
import TheShapeOfIt from '../../components/contact/TheShapeOfIt.astro';
import ContactQuestions from '../../components/contact/ContactQuestions.astro';

import Testimonials from '../../components/Testimonials.astro';
import VerifySection from '../../components/VerifySection.astro';
import FinalCTA from '../../components/FinalCTA.astro';

const title = 'Visitation, Phones & Staying in Contact | Buena Vista Health & Recovery, Chandler AZ';
const description =
  'Phone access in the evenings once you are in residential, and visiting on Wednesday, Saturday and Sunday. What contact with family looks like during treatment. Call (888) 362-5576.';

const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: [
    ['Can I keep my phone in rehab at Buena Vista?',
     'Yes, once you are in residential treatment. Phone and electronics access opens up in the evenings, every night. During medical detox phones are generally set aside, which is a matter of days rather than the whole stay.'],
    ['When can family visit?',
     'Visiting runs three days a week during the residential stay — Wednesday, Saturday and Sunday. Current times are confirmed on the admissions call.'],
    ['Why are phones restricted during detox?',
     'The first days are physically demanding and largely spent resting, and outside contact tends to make that harder. Anything genuinely urgent still reaches the person through the facility.'],
    ['Can a sponsor visit during treatment?',
     'Yes. Sponsors can come into the facility and do step work with a resident during their stay.'],
  ].map(([q, a]) => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: q,
    acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: a },
  })),
};
---
<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <TopBar />
  <Nav />

  <ContactHero />
  <TheShapeOfIt />
  <Testimonials />
  <VerifySection />
  <ContactQuestions />

  <FinalCTA />

  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)} is:inline />
</Layout>
